## 2. Agent Deliverables Forensic Audit

### 2.1 mcode Deliverables (Non-Linear SMT Engine & Assertion Elision)
- Prover Architecture: ooda/oodac/smt_poly_interval.oo:101-178 implements saturated 64-bit interval arithmetic and dedicated squaring (x^2 >= 0).
- Negative Counterexamples: Prover failed closed on 5 hostile unsatisfiable contracts (fixtures/m1_neg_square_req.oo, m1_neg_square_spec.oo, m1_neg_sign_product.oo, m1_neg_interval_bound.oo, m1_neg_ensures_unsat.oo) with exit code 1 (ERR smt unsat).
- Static Assertion Elision: ooda/oodac/c_emit_contract.oo:156-162 emits #define OO_ENS_CHECK(__result) (1) for proven postconditions, removing runtime branch overhead in generated C code.
- Deficiency: ooda/oodac/smt_clause_query.oo:71-109 evaluates only 3-token atomic clauses; compound contracts (requires x > 10 && x < 5) bypass SMT refinement and pass ooda check.

### 2.2 vibe Deliverables (Smoke Test Rail & Double-Run Law)
- Stub Inventory: 12,478 of 12,519 files (99.67%) in ooda/fixtures/*smoke*.oo derive from _template_smoke.oo. 12,503 files (99.87%) contain zero assertions and unconditionally print OK.
- Batch Execution: Stratified execution of 648 smoke fixtures across 173 domains yielded a 73.15% failure rate (306 compile errors, 168 runtime errors).
- Dogfight Runner Falsification: TEST_READY.md claimed 100.0% verification (47/47 suites passed). Direct execution of run_all_dogfight_tests.oo failed with exit code 1 (unused variable errors in test_t2_f07:64 and test_t2_f13:61). All 47 suites use in-file mocks with 0 stdlib imports and contain 124 tautological assertions.

### 2.3 grok Deliverables (Bare-Metal Toolchains)
- AMD64 System V ABI: ooda/oodac/x86_abi_classify.oo and x86_abi_sret.oo correctly lower multi-register (%rax, %rdx) and (%rax, %xmm0) pairs and hidden pointer %rdi SRet returns for >16-byte structs.
- AArch64 & Mach-O: test_a64_pure_sret.oo and test_aarch64_elf_pure.oo verify X8 SRet handling and 64KB PT_LOAD ELF64 packaging. macho_bin_emit.oo emits valid 64-bit Mach-O binaries with LC_SEGMENT_64 and LC_MAIN. All native tests execute without libc.

### 2.4 Web Platform Deliverables (openOODA.github.io)
- Static Site Generator: build_ssg.py compiles 20 pre-rendered static HTML routes with Schema.org JSON-LD structured metadata (SoftwareApplication, WebApplication, TechArticle).
- Canvas HUD Simulation: app.js renders 7 aircraft generations and Gen 7 relativistic swarm kinematics with zero heap allocations per tick via Float32Array ring buffers. 185/188 test cases pass (98.4%).
- Documentation Drift: guide/Limits.oot describes a production LLVM SSA optimizer in std/compile/llvm_codegen/, whereas SHIPPED.oot:33-46 proves production LLVM emits textual IR directly to host clang.

## 3. Negative-Trust Falsification & Security Invariants

### 3.1 Concurrency and Async Runtime Stubs
- Mock Async API: runtime/chs_rt_crypto.c:258-272 implements async_spawn_internal and async_join_internal as string transformers ("thread#" and "task_done:") without spawning OS threads.
- Thread No-Ops: runtime/chs_rt_thread.c:11-16 and chs_rt_actor.c:25-29 execute dummy usleep(10000) no-op loops.
- ThreadSanitizer Leak: Running test_tsan_bin reports exit code 66 with WARNING: ThreadSanitizer: thread leak in pthread_create at chs_rt_actor.c:72.

### 3.2 Arena Concurrency Races & Message Leaks
- Unsynchronized Arenas: runtime/chs_rt_arena.c:7-16 defines 8 fixed slots in g_ar without mutex synchronization. Running test_arena_race_bin under ThreadSanitizer reports 24 data races on g_ar.
- Queue Leaks: Channels (chs_rt_channel.c, 16 slots) and actors (chs_rt_actor.c, 16 slots) lack destruction functions, permanently leaking unconsumed queue messages.

### 3.3 Ambient Authority Bypass & Capability Signature Acceptance
- Universal Grant Injection: ooda/oodac/c_emit_fn.oo:158-163 automatically injects all capability grant calls into main(), disabling default Seccomp network and process execution filters.
- Forged Signature Acceptance: runtime/chs_rt_crypto.c:284-288 (oo_cg_verify) ignores the signature argument and returns 1, accepting forged capability signatures (0xDEADBEEFCAFE).
- File Confinement: runtime/chs_rt_fs.c:47-60 (oo_read_file) reads arbitrary host filesystem paths (/etc/os-release) without directory jail enforcement.

### 3.4 AddressSanitizer Profiles
- Core ARC Memory: All core milestone suites (test_m1 through test_m5), string ARC (chs_rt_str.c), and cycle collection (chs_rt_cycle.c) pass AddressSanitizer with 0 leaks, 0 double-frees, and 0 UB flags.
- Raw Allocator Defect: runtime/chs_rt_alloc.c:180 reads hdr->magic after OS free(), causing an ASan heap-use-after-free trap on double-free execution.

## 4. Physical & Mathematical Invariance Gaps

1. RK4 Constant Acceleration: std/phys/physics/rk4_integrator.oo:108-168 reuses constant initial acceleration across all four Runge-Kutta stages (k1..k4), reducing integration accuracy to a velocity-Verlet predictor.
2. Navier-Stokes Pressure Poisson: std/phys/continuum/navier_stokes.oo:130-183 updates 2D momentum with explicit central differencing but omits a pressure Poisson solver, violating mass conservation div(u) = 0.
3. Van der Waals Virial Inversion: std/phys/thermo/van_der_waals.oo:110-118 returns +b at T <= 1e-6 K instead of diverging to -infinity, producing an unphysical sign inversion.
4. Fresnel Polarization Phase: std/phys/optics/fresnel.oo:135-147 sets real amplitude 1.0 under Total Internal Reflection, discarding complex phase shift angles (delta_s, delta_p).
5. Astrodynamics Placeholder Stubs: Exactly 69 files in std/phys/astro_advanced/ and std/phys/astrodynamics/ contain non-functional placeholder bodies returning constant integer (return 2;).
6. Relativity Clamping & Unit Scaling: std/phys/physics/relativity.oo:21 silently clamps beta >= 1.0 to 0.999999999999c rather than failing closed; std/phys/aero/boyd_em.oo:43 uses an empirical 850.0 scaling multiplier.

## 5. Verification Reproduction Commands & Enforcer Attestation

To reproduce all forensic audit findings across subsystems:

```bash
# 1. Verify SMT non-linear interval prover and fail-closed refusal
./ooda/oodac/oodac check ooda/fixtures/m1_neg_square_req.oo
./ooda/oodac/oodac check ooda/fixtures/m1_neg_sign_product.oo

# 2. Verify Bare-Metal x86_64 and AArch64 SRet ABI classification
./ooda/oodac/oodac emit-c ooda/tests/adversarial_x86/test_m2_abi_sret.oo > /tmp/sret.c && gcc -O2 /tmp/sret.c ooda/runtime/chs_rt.c -Iooda/runtime -o /tmp/sret -lm -ldl -lpthread && /tmp/sret

# 3. Verify ThreadSanitizer data races in linear bump arenas
clang -fsanitize=thread -g -Iruntime qa/tests_falsification/test_arena_race.c runtime/chs_rt.c -lpthread -lm -lssl -lcrypto -o /tmp/tsan_race && /tmp/tsan_race

# 4. Verify capability forgery acceptance and ambient authority leak
clang -g -Iruntime qa/tests_falsification/test_ambient_authority_falsification.c runtime/chs_rt.c -lpthread -lm -lssl -lcrypto -o /tmp/ambient && /tmp/ambient

# 5. Verify AddressSanitizer cleanliness on core milestone suites
clang -fsanitize=address -g -O1 -Iooda/runtime tests/test_m1_aero_core.oo.bin.tmp.c ooda/runtime/chs_rt.c -lm -ldl -lpthread -o /tmp/m1_asan && ASAN_OPTIONS="detect_leaks=1" /tmp/m1_asan

# 6. Verify Web Platform static generation and test matrix
cd openOODA.github.io && python3 build_ssg.py && python3 tests/run_tests.py && cd ..

# 7. Execute Master Governance Enforcer (8/8 Gates)
./enforcer
```

Enforcer Attestation: Standalone binary ./enforcer executes all 8 strategic governance gates (forbidden file extensions, <=256 line limits, zero intermediate artifacts in std/, 4-element Academy headers, zero loose root files, zero struct trailing commas, RFC compliance, compiler binary separation) and terminates with 0 violations (exit code 0).
